1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,415
You walk into a room and feel every eye land on you.

2
00:00:03,675 --> 00:00:08,655
Here is the quiet truth. Almost no one is watching you as closely as you think.

3
00:00:08,915 --> 00:00:15,545
Psychologists call it the spotlight effect, the sense that our actions are noticed far more than they really are.

4
00:00:15,805 --> 00:00:24,275
In one study, students wore an embarrassing shirt and guessed that nearly half the room would notice. The real number was closer to a fifth.

5
00:00:24,535 --> 00:00:29,790
The mind places you at the center of a stage that, for everyone else, does not exist.

6
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:35,210
Each person is the star of their own spotlight, far too busy in it to study yours.

7
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:40,530
Which means the fear that freezes you is built on an audience that is not looking.

8
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:45,155
Notice the spotlight the next time it falls. Then step through it anyway.
